      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right that we should be careful whether a malformed request could possibly overflow `tx_buffer`.\n\nActually, since each sub-sequence always clocks out bits, and optionally records bits, the size of the recording cannot exceed the size of the original USB request.  Therefore, I do not believe it is possible to make this code write beyond the bounds of `tx_buffer`.  (It is possible to make it deadlock, probably, by beginning a request that is longer than the space in rx_buffer, but that gets into how the queue framework is used, and I want to get rid of that altogether, as discussed in the other CL.)",
